  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="43">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 43</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gyf gehadod man hine forwyrce mid deaðscylde, gewylde hine man ⁊ healde to bisceopes dome, be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe seo dæd si.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43" corresp="#wit-a">Gif hadod man hine forwyrce mid deaðscylde, gewylde man hine ⁊ healde to byscopes dome, be þam syo dæde sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="43" corresp="#wit-q">Si quis ordinatus se forisfaciat in morte plectendis actibus, capiatur et seruetur episcopi iudicio discutiendus, secundum quod factum sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="43" corresp="#wit-b">Gyf gehadod man hine forwyrce mid deaðscylde, gewylde man hine ⁊ healde to ðæs bisceopes dome, be ðam ðe seo dæd sy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">If a man in holy orders places his life in jeopardy by committing a capital crime, he shall be arrested, and his case shall be reserved for the bishop's decision, according to the nature of the deed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn ein geweihter Mann sich [sein Leben] verwirkt durch Todes [würdige] Schuld, ergreife und bewahre man ihn für des Bischofs Urtheilsspruch, je nachdem die Missethat ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a man in orders forfeits himself by a capital offence, let him be seized and held for the bishop's judgment, according to what the deed is.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares EGu 4.2.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
